/-!
# Source-aligned large-`b` Lemma 6.9 to Equation (32)

In Proposition 6.6(A), the large-`b` branch applies Lemma 6.9 to the outer
family `W'` of `a x b x 1` planks.  It does not apply the slab estimate to the
original family of `delta`-tubes.  This file records that object alignment.

The first theorem applies the existing callback-free thresholded Cordoba
estimate directly to the exact normalized selected-occurrence outer family.
All angle labels, pair-overlap estimates and row hulls are generated by the
certified plank theorem.  Its only numerical premise is the paper's final
`a^(-8 eta)` payment, displayed without cancellation.

The second theorem composes this genuine outer estimate with the existing
Equation (44) actual-average product and the Equation (46) inner estimate.
The remaining outer scalar comparison is explicit.  No `ActualTubeDatum`,
same-object union floor, or tube-cardinality volume upper bound is used.
-/

open Set MeasureTheory
open scoped BigOperators ENNReal NNReal

namespace Family8SelectedOccurrenceLargeBLemma69Eq32ComposerV1

open LeanEval.Analysis.WangZahlKakeya
open Submission.Kakeya.ConvexGeometry
open Submission.Kakeya.ConvexFactoring
open Submission.Kakeya.ConvexFactoring.FactoringMultiplicityAssembly
open Submission.Kakeya.ConvexFactoring.FullConvexMaximalDensity
